    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0530" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72110/9045</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-01T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 1, 1.53
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. For the President:</p>
                <p>We made satisfactory progress this morning regarding terms for German armistice.
                    Both Clemenceau and George now moderate as Foch will permit. They realize that the terms
                    [are] somewhat harsher than is necessary to fulfill your conditions regarding
                    the making of it impossible for Germany to renew hostilities. We are modifying
                    the naval program in the interest of commerce.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
